      "payload": "{\"model_calls\":1,\"phase\":\"synthesis\",\"plan\":{\"A\":\"Research memory layout and temporal locality. Produce a separable contiguous-storage variant for integration with C's fastest solver; retain row views, disjoint buffers and identical fixed boundaries. Investigate alignment or padded strides only with valid allocation and indexing guarantees. Keep 34601f00961a45b8's paired-sweep implementation as a serial alternative, not an assumed parallel improvement. Preserve separate convergence flags for both logical steps, retain the intermediate result when step one converges, and handle an odd final iteration. Its in-place, one-row-lag traversal must not be parallelized by simply distributing rows: partition boundaries introduce overwrite hazards. Prioritize measuring simple layout integration before more complex temporal blocking.\",\"B\":\"Research the SIMD row kernel and convergence-check cost, using 210ac2a977b345af as the reference. Transfer truthful restrict qualifications and row-local integer OR reductions into a C-compatible kernel without changing floating-point evaluation order. Test an exact shortcut: once a worker has detected a change during a sweep, subsequent rows may omit error calculations while still computing every stencil value. Reset this condition every logical sweep; never skip a required stopping decision. As a separate, lower-priority experiment, investigate standard output buffering or bounded chunk formatting using the same libc conversion. Preserve every formatted value, trailing space and newline. Report kernel and output changes separately; output dominance has not been measured.\",\"C\":\"Research persistent-team efficiency from ea17045cdcaa474d. Preserve contiguous worker ranges, thread-local buffer swaps, alternating padded convergence slots and one barrier per sweep. Document why each epoch remains readable until all consumers finish, why neighboring stencil writes are visible, and why every worker makes the same stopping decision. Retain 417dcccd46004b5e as the simpler synchronization fallback. Within the fixed four-core target and OpenMP runtime limits, investigate worker counts and a genuine serial path for insufficient work, using general workload thresholds rather than recognizing test inputs. Respect the actual team size and allocation-failure fallback. Do not remove synchronization required by Jacobi dependencies or replace it with unproven spinning.\",\"G\":\"Use ea17045cdcaa474d, commit a280a9056cdc3295ee385d5f56cefdb3ce1a89b3, as the initial measured incumbent. Integrate programs selectively, not by concatenating overlapping diffs. First evaluate C plus B's kernel changes and C plus A's layout changes independently; combine them only after observing their individual effects. Evaluate output changes separately. Keep A's paired-sweep solver as an optional serial alternative only if a general dispatch policy improves measured end-to-end performance; do not transplant its in-place traversal into parallel row partitions without a dependency-safe design. Compare every integration against the best standalone candidate using the unchanged validation, measurement procedure and budget. Retain the incumbent when a combination regresses or its correctness is unresolved. Record exact retained transformations and measured results. Review tiny grids, nonpositive iteration caps, buffer parity, first-step convergence and fixed boundaries without changing tests, oracle, compiler, target or permissions.\",\"analysis\":\"Only Problem E and src/laplace_seq.c are relevant. The baseline is 85.85 ms; the fastest observed C program is 44.12 ms, about 1.95x faster. The simpler persistent-team C variant takes 47.19 ms, A's paired-sweep variant 57.08 ms, and B's SIMD-plus-swap variant 58.11 ms. These favor copy elimination, SIMD and persistent parallelism, but do not isolate every transformation. Small timing differences lack uncertainty estimates, and no integration measurements establish additive gains. All roles must preserve the source's synchronous Jacobi computation: initial heat only, unchanged boundaries, original addition order and double precision, strict comparison against the original 1.0e-5f threshold, and the completed sweep at the first convergence decision or iteration limit. Preserve zero-iteration behavior and exact '%lf ' output with row newlines. Use source-level improvements on the fixed four-core ARM64 target; no expected-answer substitution, test-value specialization or experiment-setting changes.\"},\"request_sha256\":\"18c75ce4b57edb85ecdeda0eb77f77601428683a5da58fb3d8986411c5dc2479\",\"response\":{\"data\":{\"A\":\"Research memory layout and temporal locality. Produce a separable contiguous-storage variant for integration with C's fastest solver; retain row views, disjoint buffers and identical fixed boundaries. Investigate alignment or padded strides only with valid allocation and indexing guarantees. Keep 34601f00961a45b8's paired-sweep implementation as a serial alternative, not an assumed parallel improvement. Preserve separate convergence flags for both logical steps, retain the intermediate result when step one converges, and handle an odd final iteration. Its in-place, one-row-lag traversal must not be parallelized by simply distributing rows: partition boundaries introduce overwrite hazards. Prioritize measuring simple layout integration before more complex temporal blocking.\",\"B\":\"Research the SIMD row kernel and convergence-check cost, using 210ac2a977b345af as the reference. Transfer truthful restrict qualifications and row-local integer OR reductions into a C-compatible kernel without changing floating-point evaluation order. Test an exact shortcut: once a worker has detected a change during a sweep, subsequent rows may omit error calculations while still computing every stencil value. Reset this condition every logical sweep; never skip a required stopping decision. As a separate, lower-priority experiment, investigate standard output buffering or bounded chunk formatting using the same libc conversion. Preserve every formatted value, trailing space and newline. Report kernel and output changes separately; output dominance has not been measured.\",\"C\":\"Research persistent-team efficiency from ea17045cdcaa474d. Preserve contiguous worker ranges, thread-local buffer swaps, alternating padded convergence slots and one barrier per sweep. Document why each epoch remains readable until all consumers finish, why neighboring stencil writes are visible, and why every worker makes the same stopping decision. Retain 417dcccd46004b5e as the simpler synchronization fallback. Within the fixed four-core target and OpenMP runtime limits, investigate worker counts and a genuine serial path for insufficient work, using general workload thresholds rather than recognizing test inputs. Respect the actual team size and allocation-failure fallback. Do not remove synchronization required by Jacobi dependencies or replace it with unproven spinning.\",\"G\":\"Use ea17045cdcaa474d, commit a280a9056cdc3295ee385d5f56cefdb3ce1a89b3, as the initial measured incumbent. Integrate programs selectively, not by concatenating overlapping diffs. First evaluate C plus B's kernel changes and C plus A's layout changes independently; combine them only after observing their individual effects. Evaluate output changes separately. Keep A's paired-sweep solver as an optional serial alternative only if a general dispatch policy improves measured end-to-end performance; do not transplant its in-place traversal into parallel row partitions without a dependency-safe design. Compare every integration against the best standalone candidate using the unchanged validation, measurement procedure and budget. Retain the incumbent when a combination regresses or its correctness is unresolved. Record exact retained transformations and measured results. Review tiny grids, nonpositive iteration caps, buffer parity, first-step convergence and fixed boundaries without changing tests, oracle, compiler, target or permissions.\",\"analysis\":\"Only Problem E and src/laplace_seq.c are relevant. The baseline is 85.85 ms; the fastest observed C program is 44.12 ms, about 1.95x faster. The simpler persistent-team C variant takes 47.19 ms, A's paired-sweep variant 57.08 ms, and B's SIMD-plus-swap variant 58.11 ms. These favor copy elimination, SIMD and persistent parallelism, but do not isolate every transformation. Small timing differences lack uncertainty estimates, and no integration measurements establish additive gains. All roles must preserve the source's synchronous Jacobi computation: initial heat only, unchanged boundaries, original addition order and double precision, strict comparison against the original 1.0e-5f threshold, and the completed sweep at the first convergence decision or iteration limit. Preserve zero-iteration behavior and exact '%lf ' output with row newlines. Use source-level improvements on the fixed four-core ARM64 target; no expected-answer substitution, test-value specialization or experiment-setting changes.\"},\"error\":null,\"infrastructure_error\":false,\"model\":\"gpt-6-astra\",\"nonce\":\"5155afbdffc34f5cb7dce5ca2b8af5fc\",\"protocol\":\"hpc-forest-codex-mailbox-v1\",\"reasoning_effort\":\"xhigh\",\"request_sha256\":\"18c75ce4b57edb85ecdeda0eb77f77601428683a5da58fb3d8986411c5dc2479\",\"session_id\":\"2bd8b683b45b41c8b48ec38708f46bab\",\"usage\":{\"cached_tokens_included_in_input\":true,\"codex_jsonl_sha256\":\"e9b89331ab2d5460c91d80aa5d6533cb1849c39c6b717e7c3a926a0be13f0d59\",\"events\":[{\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"cached_input_tokens\":0,\"input_tokens\":20581,\"output_tokens\":4953,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":4092}],\"llm_calls\":1,\"model_requested\":\"gpt-6-astra\",\"reasoning_effort_requested\":\"xhigh\",\"token_accounting\":\"exact\",\"tokens\":25534,\"tool_events\":[]}},\"status\":\"complete\"}",
